			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Consolidate window message handling and robust URI resolution\n\nMigrate all window message variants (Info, Warning, Error) to a single `Window.ShowMessage` gRPC method, delegating level-specific logic and action button rendering to the Mountain backend. This replaces the previous fragmented approach of direct RPC calls and local workarounds, ensuring consistent behavior where action button selections correctly propagate back to the extension host.\n\nSimultaneously, enhance the URI resolution logic in the routing handler to robustly construct URL strings for icon assets. The new logic explicitly checks for `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties to handle complex `Uri` objects (including light/dark theme variants) when standard string conversion fails, preventing broken icon paths in the editor UI.\n\nUpdate internal service references to use the unified `MountainClient` instance. Impact: Restores reliable user interaction flows for dialogs and ensures visual fidelity for file system icons during RPC serialization.",
			"SHA": "d23b9bd3459c1ab81baa60c29d94d00bc3c0c8b9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:36:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Correct Terminal RPC method naming to match Vine proto\n\nUpdate the gRPC request string for terminal creation in `Services/Terminal/Service.ts` from `\"terminal.create\"` to `\"$terminal:create\"`. This aligns the invocation with the exact PascalCase and namespace-prefixed definition in the `Vine.proto` specification.\n\nThe previous lowercase dot-notation format is inconsistent with the strongly-typed IPC contract established for the Mountain backend, potentially causing method resolution failures. This change ensures the `Create` operation is correctly routed to the terminal handler in the extension host.\n\nImpact: Restores reliable terminal instance creation via the gRPC bridge.",
			"SHA": "d6c9004c8f04387f4a4ca37e1aea56a262e681f5"
		}
	],
